==History==
2016
*The Tornado [[Cards|card]] was added to the game on 11/11/2016.
*On 15/12/2016, the [[Version History#December 2016 Update (15/12/2016)|December 2016 Update]], increased its area radius to 5.5 tiles (from 5 tiles) and increased its pulling power to 220% (from 60%). This update also changed its description. It used to say: "''Drags enemy troops to the center of the Tornado while dealing damage over time. Doesn't affect buildings.''"
2017
*On 13/3/2017, the [[Version History#March 2017 Update (13/3/2017)|March 2017 Update]], allowed the Tornado to be placed on [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]].
*On 12/6/2017, a [[Version History#June 2017 Update (12/6/2017)|June 2017 Update]], decreased the Tornado's duration to 2.55 seconds (from 3.05 seconds), but allowed multiple Tornado [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] to stack.
2018
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]], increased the Tornado‘s damage per second by 21%, but also decreased the duration to 2.05 seconds (from 2.55 seconds). It also allowed the Tornado to be placed on the river.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Tornado from Builder's Workshop to Frozen Peak.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8).
*On 1/10/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (1/10/2018)|Balance Update]], fixed a bug where [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that were spawned after their parent troops died would be immune to [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] damage.
2019
*On 28/1/2019, the [[Version History#January%202019%20Update%20(28/1/2019)|January 2019 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Tornado from Frozen Peak to Spell Valley.
2020
*On 5/5/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (5/5/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Tornado's duration to 1.05 second (from 2.05 seconds), increased its pulling power to 360% (from 220%), and increased its damage by 100%. It was also changed to damage buildings. As a result, the "''Doesn't affect buildings.''" line from its description was removed.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Tornado from Spell Valley to Legendary Arena. It also added a card render to the Tornado's card info screen.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
*On 15/11/2021, a [[Version History#Minor%20Update%20(15/11/2021)|Minor Update]], allowed the Tornado to deal damage to {{Rarity|Champion}} cards when they activate their ability.
2022
*On 30/3/2022, the [[Version History#Miner%20Update%20(30/3/2022)|Miner Update]], fixed an issue where troops could sometimes ignore the pull effect of Tornado.
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Tornado from Legendary Arena to Miner's Mine.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14). It also fixed an issue with some cards continuing to attack [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]] after being pulled out of range by Tornado.
2025
*On 4/2/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/2/2025)|Balance Update]], made it so that [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Lumberjack Ghost]] is immune to Tornado.
*On 9/4/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (9/4/2025)|Balance Update]], increased the Tornado's attack time interval to 0.55 seconds (from 0.5 seconds).

