==Trivia== 
*The word "''Tornado''" comes from the Latin "''tonare''" (tonō), meaning 'to thunder'.
**In the Chinese language settings of the game, the Tornado's name translates to "Hurricane Spell".
*The Tornado is the only spell from Clash Royale to inspire a trap in Clash of Clans, that being the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Tornado_Trap Tornado Trap].
*The Tornado has the largest area of effect, with a radius of 5.5 tiles. This means that it is also the only card that can affect all 3 [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]] at once.
*The Tornado is 1 of 4 damaging [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] cards that does not contain the phrase "''Reduced damage to Crown Towers.''" in its description despite dealing reduced damage to Crown Towers, with the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Goblin Curse]], and [[Rage]].
*The Tornado is 1 of 7 spells which have team-colored rings on their radius, the others are Earthquake, [[Freeze]], [[Poison]], Rage, [[Clone]], [[Graveyard]], and [[Goblin Curse]].
*The card image shows a tornado with a pig being sucked into the tornado. On its card render, 2 [[Royal Hogs]] are featured in the tornado's vicinity.
*The original concept for the Tornado was a [https://youtu.be/aFrk-wDjJ4w?t=301 Butterfly] spell that was used for distracting [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]]. However, it was replaced with the Tornado due to visual problems.
*It appeared in the picture for the balance changes in the [[Version History#November 2016 Update (1/11/2016)|November 2016 Update]] before it was officially announced that it was going to be added to the game.
*The Tornado was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Tornado was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/psZXKWHkKkE?si=PbjvbZt8stghz6eJ King's Cup II Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
**The Tornado was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/C5qBcdcErfM?si=e37mhAgNKAA5kMJI Clash Royale League 2018 Tournament], by a player called Lciop.
**The Tornado was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/cmBlEI-aDoo?si=UoD1Sit2YvQR19xs Clash Royale League 2019 Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
**The Tornado was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/pRfrjMiHbQA?si=P2kVLJUlXH1SZoHm Clash Royale League 2021 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
*The Tornado has had balance changes that were planned for it but were not added to the game. More specifically: 
**The initial balance change for Tornado on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (5/5/2020)|5/5/2020 balance changes]] was a pull power increase to 440% (from 220%), but it was lowered to 360% [https://twitter.com/ClashRoyale/status/1257611280267063302 last minute].
**On 7/2/2023, the Tornado was supposed to receive a 6% damage decrease, but this change [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-44-balance-wip was pulled back last minute].

